      },
      "message": "feat(ui): the Recipes tab explains recipes, stars the stock material, derives Vc and fz\n\nU11 of the tool library refit. The Recipes tab opens with one line\nthat says what a recipe is and which row operations take. A star\nmarks the row of the stock material in force (the setup stock's,\nelse the document's). Under the table, one line for each row gives\nits surface speed and chip load; the lines are cached with their\ninput, so a still frame computes nothing. The buttons Add material…,\nSuggest feeds and speeds and Copy recipes from tool… stand on one\nrow, with a units note. Each one writes the window's draft; the one\nApply lands it as one ChangeTool undo step.\n\nFixes #4337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
